      "value": "@{5a4aaf7f758fa46d131cd36b|full_name}: Of course it is. There's one thing called encryption which makes it significantly harder to read a file, any coder should know about it and it's not too hard to do. Do you know what VRChat does? They randomly rename the files. With enough time, you can get every avatar you've come across because all of it is saved in your cache folder. At least the models, which is bad enough.",
